# P13-011 implementation plan: sparse difflist on sample-sharded reads

**For agentic workers:** execute task-by-task via subagent-driven development. A fresh
implementer per task, a fresh reviewer before the next starts, then a whole-branch
review. Steps use `- [ ]`.

**Goal:** the per-sample carrier / burden query on a sample-sharded (`IsConcat`) cohort
uses the pgenlib difflist (sparse) decode, which is force-disabled today.

**Architecture:** add a combined-carrier-list method to `ConcatPgenReader`; flip the
`!IsConcat()` exclusion at `pfile_reader.cpp:3936`; wire the concat branch into the
sparse Phase-1 scan. Read-side only.

**Tech stack:** C++ DuckDB extension, pgenlib (`third_party/plink-ng`), sqllogictest
`.test` files, DuckDB v2.0.0 only.

**Spec:** `docs/planning/P13-011-concat-sparse-difflist` (read it — it carries the
design, the measured ceiling, §5 correctness requirements, §7 test method, §8 Review
Focus). Branch `feat/concat-sparse` off `e484213`.

## Global Constraints

- DuckDB **v2.0.0 only**. No v1.5 compatibility shim needed.
- **Never commit `third_party/plink-ng`** — the CMake configure patches it (a 0-line
  diff, pgenlib_read.cc VFS shim); it shows dirty, pointer unchanged. Exclude it from
  every commit.
- `clang-format` clean (`make format-fix`), or Format CI reddens.
- Match surrounding conventions: the `Get*` methods, `OrBitsAtOffset`, `EnsureScratch`,
  `AlignedBuffer`, the `make_uniq<Member>` pattern.
- Do not touch the shared `main` worktree. Work only in `trees/feat-concat-sparse`.
- Build on Slurm `batch` (cold build needs > 30 min): `srun -n 1 -c 12 --mem=24G -p
  batch -t 90 bash -lc 'VCPKG_TOOLCHAIN_PATH=$HOME/vcpkg/scripts/buildsystems/vcpkg.cmake
  GEN=ninja make release'`. Later incremental builds fit `ci` (`-t 30`).
- A **new** `.test` file is discovered only at configure/build time; editing an existing
  one needs no rebuild. So build after adding the new `.test`.

## Review Focus (spec §8 — each pinned by a task's tests)

- ALT-major re-decode binds the shard's reader (`m.pgr`/`m.pssi`/`m.out_ct`), not
  lstate's (§5.3). — Task 2
- Combined carrier list sized to `OutputSampleCt()`, not `osc/8` (§5.2). — Task 2
- Per-shard threshold `max(1, m.out_ct/8)`, not combined (§5.1). — Task 2
- The proof-ran mechanism flips between concat sparse and dense (§6). — Task 1 proves it
  on single-file; Task 2 flips it on concat.
- `g==3` (missing) on both difflist and dense-fallback paths (§5.5). — Task 2, F2/fixtures
- Per-sample `EXCEPT`, not sum equality — an offset bug preserves sums (§7). — Task 1
  writes the harness; Task 2 turns it green.

